## Engram Persistent Memory — Protocol

You have access to Engram persistent memory via MCP tools (`mem_save`, `mem_search`, `mem_context`, `mem_session_summary`, etc.).

### WHEN TO SAVE (mandatory)

Call `mem_save` IMMEDIATELY after: bug fixes, architecture/design decisions, non-obvious discoveries, config/environment changes, patterns, or user preferences.

Format:
- **title**: Verb + what (short, searchable)
- **type**: bugfix | decision | architecture | discovery | pattern | config | preference
- **scope**: project (default) | personal
- **topic_key** (recommended for evolving topics)
- **content**: What / Why / Where / Learned

### WHEN TO SEARCH

On "remember" / "recall" / "qué hicimos" / past work: `mem_context` → `mem_search` → `mem_get_observation`.
Also search proactively when starting related work.

### SESSION CLOSE (mandatory)

Before ending a session, call `mem_session_summary` with Goal, Instructions, Discoveries, Accomplished, Next Steps, Relevant Files.

### AFTER COMPACTION

Call `mem_context` to recover state before continuing.

### PASSIVE CAPTURE

End task responses with `## Key Learnings:` numbered items when useful.
